lscpu Displays CPU architecture information.
lsblk -a Lists all block devices, including empty devices.
free Displays physical and swap-memory usage.
free -m Displays memory usage in mebibytes.
df Reports filesystem disk-space usage.
df -h Reports filesystem usage in human-readable units.
du filename Shows disk usage for a file; recursively summarizes a directory.
du -sh filename Shows only the human-readable total disk usage.
cat /proc/cpuinfo Displays detailed CPU information exposed by the kernel.
cat /proc/meminfo Displays detailed memory information exposed by the kernel.
sudo fdisk -l Lists detected disks and their partition tables.
fdisk -s /dev/partition Displays a partition size in blocks on systems that support this legacy option.
